# 9. And finally the boot process

Now everything connects to the boot flow you were asking about earlier:

```text
Power ON
   │
   ▼
TI AM3358 Boot ROM
   │
   ▼
MLO / SPL
   │
   ▼
U-Boot
   │
   ├── loads Linux Kernel
   ├── loads Device Tree
   │
   ▼
Linux Kernel
   │
   ▼
Mount ROOTFS
   │
   ▼
systemd
   │
   ▼
box-storage.service
   │
   ▼
/opt/box-storage/bin/boxes
   │
   ▼
main()
   │
   ▼
BoxManager
   │
   ├──────────────┐
   ▼              ▼
StaticBox     DynamicBox
   │              │
   └──────┬───────┘
          ▼
   Date Indexed Data
```

### The key concept

**`boot/` = "How do I start Linux?"**

**`rootfs/` = "Once Linux starts, what environment and applications do I have?"**

**`app/` = "What did we develop?"**

**`config/` = "How should our application behave?"**

**`deployment/` = "How do we put everything onto the BeagleBone?"**

And **Yocto is the system that ultimately brings the BSP, kernel, bootloader, root filesystem, and your application together into a deployable image.**

